  "title": "Erdős Problem #863",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r\\geq 2$ and let $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ be a set of maximal size such that there are at most $r$ solutions to $n=a+b$ with $a\\leq b$ for any $n$. (That is, $A$ is a $B_2[r]$ set.)\nSimilarly, let $B\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ be a set of maximal size such that there are at most $r$ solutions to $n=a-b$ for any $n$.\nIf $\\lvert A\\rvert\\sim c_rN^{1/2}$ as $N\\to \\infty$ and $\\lvert B\\rvert \\sim c_r'N^{1/2}$ as $N\\to \\infty$ then is it true that $c_r\neq c_r'$ for $r\\geq 2$? Is it true that $c_r'<c_r$?",
    "sha256": "6ce3b6bee4bcbef03b182f989502833dd05e4a7bc9db0cdbda3d195eb12c476c",
